# 10km loop configuration. Sourced by the scripts as shell.
# Each setting can be overridden by an environment variable of the same name.
# Scripts read the copy in the central loop worktree, so changes take effect
# once a Curator has merged them into main.

# Repos are the git repos in central/; each repo's settings (branch, author,
# remotes) are in its own git config. See prompts/kickoff.md.

# The state database and the action log. Empty: <LOOP_ROOT>/.10km/loop.db, and
# actions.log next to the database. Launched agents get the same values.
MSM_DB="${MSM_DB-}"
MSM_LOG="${MSM_LOG-}"

# Seconds between Dispatcher passes (run-loop).
DISPATCH_INTERVAL="${DISPATCH_INTERVAL-60}"
# Session time-out in seconds; override per role with PLANNER_TIMEOUT,
# WORKER_TIMEOUT, CURATOR_TIMEOUT, AUDITOR_TIMEOUT.
SESSION_TIMEOUT="${SESSION_TIMEOUT-3600}"
# Seconds before SIGKILL after SIGTERM (process launcher).
KILL_GRACE="${KILL_GRACE-10}"
# Seconds after launch before a session that doesn't look alive is expired.
START_GRACE="${START_GRACE-180}"
# Maximum Workers active at once.
MAX_WORKERS="${MAX_WORKERS-4}"
# Backlog size at which the Planner prioritises or prunes.
BACKLOG_SIZE="${BACKLOG_SIZE-50}"

# Auditor: due daily after AUDIT_TIME (HH:MM) in AUDIT_TIMEZONE, or after
# AUDIT_CYCLES_LIMIT curated cycles. Empty or 0 disables a trigger. The first
# Auditor runs only after a cycle has been curated.
AUDIT_TIME="${AUDIT_TIME-07:00}"
AUDIT_TIMEZONE="${AUDIT_TIMEZONE-UTC}"
AUDIT_CYCLES_LIMIT="${AUDIT_CYCLES_LIMIT-0}"

# Stop the loop (reason "idle") after this many consecutive empty cycles.
IDLE_CYCLE_LIMIT="${IDLE_CYCLE_LIMIT-3}"

# Gates, one shell command per line. Workers run WORKER_GATES before done; the
# Curator runs VALIDATION_GATES. Non-zero exit means the gate failed.
WORKER_GATES="${WORKER_GATES-}"
VALIDATION_GATES="${VALIDATION_GATES-}"

# Notification commands, one per line, run with TENKM_PRIORITY, TENKM_TITLE,
# TENKM_BODY and TENKM_PROJECT set. Empty: append to NOTIFICATIONS.md.
NOTIFY_CMD="${NOTIFY_CMD-}"

# Launcher: "process" runs an agent command. The command runs from the session
# directory with SESSION, PROMPT_FILE and FIRST_MESSAGE set; FIRST_MESSAGE names
# the session and the prompt file. Override per role with PLANNER_AGENT,
# WORKER_AGENT, CURATOR_AGENT, AUDITOR_AGENT (e.g. to choose a model).
# Name the harness session after the loop session where the harness can (-n).
LAUNCHER="${LAUNCHER-process}"
[ -n "${LOOP_AGENT+x}" ] || LOOP_AGENT='claude --no-session-persistence --dangerously-skip-permissions -n "$SESSION" -p "$FIRST_MESSAGE"'
# LOOP_AGENT='codex exec "$FIRST_MESSAGE"'
# LOOP_AGENT='kiro-cli chat --no-interactive --trust-all-tools "$FIRST_MESSAGE"'

# The operator's agent, for kickoff and operator sessions. It runs with
# FIRST_MESSAGE set (empty for a plain session), and ONE_SHOT=1 when given a
# one-shot instruction, and SESSION set for an operator session (not kickoff).
# It doesn't fall back to LOOP_AGENT.
[ -n "${OPERATOR_AGENT+x}" ] || OPERATOR_AGENT='claude ${SESSION:+-n "$SESSION"} ${ONE_SHOT:+-p} ${FIRST_MESSAGE:+"$FIRST_MESSAGE"}'
